  "why": "Per-item states for list fields (De-Dupe UI S-41; operator 2026-11-24, option (a)). One candidate carries, per family, an item that matches, one that is merely similar or has no counterpart: directors Ann Lee (identical) and Bo Diddley (neutral); actors Jon Smyth against John Smith (0.90: similar) and Zed Nobody (neutral); countries US (identical) and GB (neutral); Alt IDs: IMDb equal with an empty relation (identical), a second IMDb value tt0000002 under that matched Kind (neutral: the comparator counts no conflict where the Kind already matched through another value), thetvdb.com value differing (mismatch, the comparator's conflict), themoviedb.org/movie with no counterpart (neutral), and an equal thetvdb.com value under IsDerivedFrom (neutral: never compared). Each list is in the candidate's record-view order. Fails if a field state is painted onto every item, if a free-text item is shown red, if a non-identity Alt ID is compared, or if an extra value under a matched Kind is called a conflict. SCOPE: the four families' item rules; not titles, not sort-name entries (the fixture format carries no sort names). CORRECTED 2026-11-25 (De-Dupe UI branch review): the first version carried no extra value under a matched Kind, so removing that rule passed it; tt0000002 was added.",
